{title: 106 Tuya es la gloria}
{key: D}
{time: 4/4}
{lyricist: Edmond Louis Budry, 1884 (1854-1932); Vers. esp.: Carlos A. Steger (1953- )}
{composer: Georg F; Handel}

{sov}
1. [D]Tuya es la gloria, [A]Cristo [D]ven[A]cedor.
[D]De la muerte invicto [Em]eres, [D]oh [A]Se[D]ñor.
[Bm]Ángeles brillantes [Em]vieron [Bm]tu [F#]esplendor,
[Bm]cuando derro[G6]taste [E7]muerte [F#m]y [Bm]do[E][E7][A]lor.
{eov}

{soc}
[D]Tuya es la gloria, [A]Cristo [D]ven[A]cedor.
[D]De la muerte invicto [Em]eres, [D]oh [A]Se[D]ñor.
{eoc}

{sov}
2. [D]Resucitado, [A]Cristo [D]el [A]Salvador,
[D]con amor invita, [Em]quita [D]el [A]te[D]mor.
[Bm]Cante hoy la iglesia [Em]cántico [Bm]triun[F#]fal;
[Bm]Cristo ha ven[G6]cido [E7]al bas[F#m]tión [Bm]mor[E][E7][A]tal.
{eov}

{sov}
3. [D]Ya no dudamos, [A]Príncipe [D]in[A]mortal:
[D]solo tú das vida, [Em]líbra[D]nos [A]del [D]mal.
[Bm]Danos la victoria [Em]por tu [Bm]amor [F#]sin par;
[Bm]llévanos a [G6]salvo [E7]al e[F#m]terno [Bm]ho[E][E7][A]gar.
{eov}
